  hero={hero}
  schema={schema}
  facts={facts}
  transport={transport}
  slider={slider}
  relatedEvents={relatedEvents}
  cta={cta}
  imageCredit={imageCredit}
>
  <p slot="intro">The Festa della Castagna is the autumn fixture of the Amalfi Coast, and in 2026 it reaches its forty-ninth edition. It takes place in Scala, the oldest village on the coast, facing Ravello across the Valle del Dragone, and fills two October weekends with a final day on the 24th.</p>
  <p slot="intro">It is run by the Scala, Città del Castagno association together with the comune. Braziers for the chestnuts are lit in the squares, stalls serve local produce and tastings, and the music runs late. This is a village festival rather than a built tourist event: most of the crowd comes from the surrounding towns.</p>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">What to expect</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The produce</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">The Scala chestnut</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">Chestnut woods cover the upper slopes of the comune between 400 and 700 metres, which is why Scala calls itself the Chestnut Town. Alongside the roasted chestnuts you will find cakes, preserves and the farm cooking of the valley.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The village</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Scala out of season</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">In October the coast empties and Scala becomes what it is, a village of a few hundred people with a Romanesque cathedral and a view of Ravello that nobody photographs. You can park, you can walk, and you do not queue.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</EventPageLayout>
